# Rank 1599 / CVE-2026-48781: Postiz's auth middleware treated the
# verified JWT payload as the user object itself, so authorization
# attributes inside the token body -- isSuperAdmin, activated -- were
# trusted without re-resolving the account (privilege escalation
# through trusted token claims, CWE-345/CWE-287; the release commit
# "feat: security fixes" also strips stored integration credentials
# -- token, refreshToken, customInstanceDetails -- from the no-auth
# integrations response, and deletes the NowPayments crypto
# endpoints). AuthMiddleware in apps/backend/src/services/auth/
# auth.middleware.ts did `let user = AuthService.verifyJWT(auth) as
# User | null;` -- the signed body becomes the User, claims and all.
# Pool commit 23696d2973 is the real fix (COMMIT_OK): the middleware
# verifies the signature only, requires payload.id, and re-resolves
# `let user = await this._userService.getUserById(payload.id)` --
# the database is the authority, the token merely names the account.
# No pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, claim-to-principal resolution. The signature check
# exists and runs -- the defect is treating the verified payload as
# the principal rather than as a lookup key, the same
# unverified-claims family as rank 1546 (rate limiting on a decoded
# claim) with the trust inverted: nothing can ask "are authorization
# attributes re-resolved from the store rather than read from the
# token" -- session-resolution vocabulary. A binding on Postiz's own
# AuthMiddleware would detect this application rather than the
# weakness. Measured on the real code: scanning auth.middleware.ts
# reports zero findings at both revisions. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry.
# No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1599 records the
# payload-as-user form and the re-resolved form, both asserting
# reject VYQL-AUTH-079: when session-resolution vocabulary lands, the
# payload-as-user form must flip to expect.

test "rank1599: the token payload becomes the user"
  lang javascript
  file apps/backend/src/services/auth/auth.middleware.ts
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  export class AuthMiddleware {
    async use(req, res, next) {
      const auth = req.cookies.auth || req.headers.authorization;
      if (!auth) {
        throw new Error('Forbidden');
      }
      try {
        let user = AuthService.verifyJWT(auth);

        if (!user) {
          throw new Error('Forbidden');
        }

        req.user = user;
        next();
      } catch (err) {
        throw new Error('Forbidden');
      }
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1599: the fix re-resolves the user from the database"
  lang javascript
  file apps/backend/src/services/auth/auth.middleware.ts
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  export class AuthMiddleware {
    constructor(userService) {
      this._userService = userService;
    }

    async use(req, res, next) {
      const auth = req.cookies.auth || req.headers.authorization;
      if (!auth) {
        throw new Error('Forbidden');
      }
      try {
        // Verify the JWT signature only. Never trust authorization-relevant
        // claims (id, isSuperAdmin, activated) from the token body — always
        // re-resolve the user from the database using the id.
        const payload = AuthService.verifyJWT(auth);

        if (!payload?.id) {
          throw new Error('Forbidden');
        }

        let user = await this._userService.getUserById(payload.id);

        if (!user) {
          throw new Error('Forbidden');
        }

        req.user = user;
        next();
      } catch (err) {
        throw new Error('Forbidden');
      }
    }
  }
  ```
